        <body>
            <div xml:id="d872">

                <pb facs="0914" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg802"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2491/92.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Chargé
                    Weitzel.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic">December 7,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wilson acknowledges the legation’s telegram of December 2, and instructs Mr.
                    Weitzel, to inform the secretary of state for foreign affairs that it was not
                    the intention of the department in either of its notes referred to to accept or
                    suggest any particular conditions of arbitration concerning the scope or form of
                    the question to be submitted, but, because of the sincere friendship of the
                    United States equally for Panama and Costa Rica, both notes were confined to
                    favoring prompt submission to the authoritative and final decision of the sole
                    arbitrator, of the respective contentions as to the boundary line, upon a
                    formulation of the question at issue by a protocol to be agreed upon between the
                    respective plenipotentiaries of those powers</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
